  "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Veris Industries E50-series DIN-rail power meters on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Veris E50B1A/E50C2A/E50C3A: 57 objects (42 AI, 15 BI), 55 polled by default. Inputs give real, apparent and reactive energy, power and PF total and per phase, voltages, currents, frequency, present and max demand and per-phase energy; binary inputs flag voltage and current out of range.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Veris_E50C2A_E50C3A_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/e50cxa_full_i0b2.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 55 of the 57 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Total Instantaneous Real Power (AI 3) carries kV as its unit in the profile as published; it is a power value."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Veris_E50C2A_E50C3A_a",
    "doc_number": "Veris_E50C2A_E50C3A_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Veris_E50C2A_E50C3A_a_LX.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Map total real power, real energy consumption and average voltage L-L first. The listed objects are read-only.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "Total Instantaneous Real Power",
        "why": "Total real power"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "RealEnergy Consumption (clear via reset register)1",
        "why": "Real energy consumption"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 7",
        "name": "Voltage L-L Averageof3Phases",
        "why": "Average voltage L-L"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 9",
        "name": "Current Average of 3 Phases",
        "why": "Average current"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 6",
        "name": "Total PowerFactor (Total KW /TotalKVA)",
        "why": "Total power factor"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 25",
        "name": "Frequency (derivedfrom Phase A)",
        "why": "Frequency"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 34",
        "name": "Total RealPower Present Demand",
        "why": "Real power present demand"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The BASgatewayLX presents each Modbus device as its own virtual BACnet device on BACnet IP; give it a unique device instance and Modbus address (serial) or IP address (Modbus TCP) when you add it with this profile.",
      "One BASgatewayLX handles up to 100 Modbus devices and 1000 polled points in total, so leave unneeded rows unpolled."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Real Energy Consumption is printed twice (AI 1 and AI 2); the register document has the two words/formats.",
      "Unpolled rows do not appear as BACnet objects until enabled in the gateway's device profile page."
    ]
  },
